Stop the session mode override synchronizer from retrying a failed override in a tight loop.

When a Copilot session starts with an --agent-mode its catalog does not allow (for example
https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/session-modes#autopilot), setSessionMode() fails on
every attempt. The released synchronizer keeps the override pending and retries it on every
metadata sync with no delay, so an idle session retries it about ten times per second and
saturates the link with session sync traffic (see BUG-session-mode-override-retry-loop.md).

This patch ports the fork's fix to the bundled CLI 0.2.20 package:
- A definitive provider rejection settles the override, is logged once, and is cleared from
  session metadata so later starts do not replay it, as the model override synchronizer does.
- Other failures keep one immediate retry, then back off exponentially from 1 s to 60 s.
- A newer override is applied at once, regardless of the backoff.

Apply from the extracted release root with patch -p1 --fuzz=0. The content-addressed chunk
name and hunks are specific to cli-v0.2.20.

Adapted from the fork's apps/cli/src/agent/runtime/sessionModeOverrideSync.ts.

